# Phase 3 remoting transport — execution log

- Session: 2026-09-27T06:39:38Z
- Scope: Continue the Java 5.5.1 write-buffer watermark parity review; no Phase 3 acceptance declaration or Phase 4 work.
- Java evidence: `NettyRemotingClient.start()` installs Netty `WriteBufferWaterMark` only when both `writeBufferLowWaterMark > 0` and `writeBufferHighWaterMark > 0`. RocketMQ's pinned Netty version is 4.1.114.Final. Its `ChannelOutboundBuffer` flips unwritable only when pending bytes become strictly greater than high, and writable only when pending bytes become strictly less than low. Unknown/non-connected channel writability behavior was already covered separately.
- Changes: `ClientConfig::validate` now applies low <= high only when both thresholds are enabled; added `write_buffer_watermarks()` to configure the connection only when both are positive. Watermark threshold transitions now use Java's strict comparisons. Extended the hysteresis test to assert equality-at-high and equality-at-low stay writable/unwritable respectively. Updated the Phase 3 inventory with enablement parity, test evidence, and the remaining difference that Rust accounts queued outbound bytes rather than Netty pending outbound bytes.
- Verification: `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --offline` (41 unit, 4 codec, 71 transport); `cargo test --workspace --offline`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings`; `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check` all passed.
- Status: Watermark code and inventory changes are not yet committed. Public API/config source/priority/effective-time inventory and remaining `PARTIAL` review remain open. Phase 3 remains unaccepted; P3-V04 remains assigned to Phase 19; no plan files changed.
